f 17592186045417] [17592186172140 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186172575 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172140 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186172576 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172140 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186535939 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172140 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186535986 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172140 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186541113 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172140 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying the Line of Reflection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172140 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186171805 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172140 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "c328605f-900a-55c9-8668-98274d655af3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172207 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186172676 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172207 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186173104 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172207 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186173105 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172207 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186173106 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172207 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172207 #edb/ref 1045 "Reflections of Figures Across Arbitrary Lines" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172207 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186173104 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172207 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050070 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172207 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172207 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "3ff5ddfd-7d5c-561b-b69a-738d96c9159a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172676 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186173106 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172676 #edb/ref 1061 10216 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172676 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0b163811-1b76-5f40-981e-e52237413897" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172676 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186173143 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173104 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186173105 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173104 #edb/ref 1061 9519 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173104 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fffdaa5e-08a2-5d55-9beb-0a54a66ab887" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173104 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186173142 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173105 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186172676 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173105 #edb/ref 1061 9532 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173105 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "74b2d07d-e9c9-51e3-8d4a-34988b9b5014" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173105 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186172139 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173106 #edb/ref 1061 9550 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173106 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3793bd1f-5ffe-57f0-b062-c596bcf497d8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173106 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186172140 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173142 #edb/ref 1064 "We can reflect an object in any line. Consider the diagram below. The two polygons are the mirror images of each other in the line $l.$\n\n![](images/1e/1e4dfb2939916df5d5018320819f14fcec261a1e77c171b551e9868a8c3bebc8.png)\n\nIf we want to reflect the quadrilateral $ABCD$ below in the line $l,$ we can reflect each vertex separately and then draw the segments between the resulting corresponding vertices.\n\n![](images/a4/a47c41b41ecae2bc4c281e1b90c843ae68fa907a0d2ff49c48454fd80e2977c7.png)\n\nLet's start by reflecting the point $A.$ To do this, we need to plot a new point $A'$ on the opposite side of $l$ at an equal distance away from $l$ as the original point $A.$\n\nThe original point $A$ is $4$ units to the left of $l,$ so we need to plot the new point $A'$ at a distance of $4$ units to the right of $l.$\n\n![](images/33/33bb82c9d0f20df13f46060b9aec21e8c4d1231766926c47b7718bf58e1c5e32.png)\n\nNow let's reflect other vertices of the quadrilateral in the same way:\n\n![](images/00/00ec763ccce462effa024486a6ff09a98b549c61179de18bb850470e835a7627.png)\n\nFinally, we draw segments between the reflected vertices.\n\n![](images/7f/7ffd0cfa45051d8376c46528370b34222a1ebb226987e7530d5081d69942bbde.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173142 #edb/ref 1065 2282 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173142 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "787862ce-3b2c-5778-b18c-dffebb58451d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173142 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173143 #edb/ref 1064 "If we're given two points, we can find the line of reflection that maps one point onto another by finding the perpendicular bisector of the segment joining the two points.\n\nFor example, suppose that the line $l$ reflects the point $A$ onto $A'$ below. How can we find the equation of $l?$\n\n![](images/79/79ddc15badc704a9c9860207a5156c3a0505ab626572581bcf3146976338a015.png)\n\nThe line $l$ is the perpendicular bisector of the line segment $\\overline{AA'}.$ So, the line of reflection is $y=-1.$\n\n![](images/aa/aa240e562acf388bdf05751e680e917bc8465bad34300334f6b423df46a7d1f3.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173143 #edb/ref 1065 2363 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173143 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "8464dac5-c554-50b1-94c2-4e8df122e9fb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173143 #edb/ref 1067 "Identifying the Line of Reflection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540525 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186541164 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540525 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186541185 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540525 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186541222 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540525 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540525 #edb/ref 1045 "Reflections of Figures Across Arbitrary Lines" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540525 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186541185 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540525 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540525 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050070 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540525 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "ce12ad27-8b43-5e90-aadb-9f6033164639" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540571 #edb/ref 1080 "images/0d/0d7d9b6f6805a5b142558d56def88d5a4088cd44b4ba59e51075a5ff683a5ba0.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540571