" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541083 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we reflect our figure in the line ${l}_{1}:$\n\n![](images/3b/3b9947ebf3ebf9d6cbd2aa14ab889eb378a3bf5a78ad78d084e2662faab4d733.png)\n\nNow, we reflect the resulting figure in the line ${l}_{2}:$ \n\n![](images/af/afe4c717eb216e75e950cce573d87f6f34f83cfe99f9b2e60c5e75f9dee7fafa.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541113 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186540985 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541113 #edb/ref 1069 "q-53354" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541113 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541113 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/e3/e3093210c2f9523999c06ffe4e03606531e81707b798bbc7278d7b28cdfe4e25.png)\n\nThe triangle $T$ is mapped to the triangle ${T}^{′}$ under the action of a reflection. What is the equation of the line of reflection?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541113 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "982b9ee4-2f8e-53f9-befc-0859353e9231" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541113 #edb/ref 1074 "The line of reflection is the perpendicular bisector of the segments joining each point to its image. \n\nTherefore, the line of reflection is $y=-2,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/7b/7b77cd63f7a93a62576846ad92b5ce2bcc1853137c5f582de42c2ebce4001892.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541164 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186541222 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541164 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "219d0137-8f2f-5553-85c0-382a2e2af841" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541164 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186541113 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541185 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186541164 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541185 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5b357e8b-8c64-56fa-a528-57e470966cd6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541185 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186541056 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541222 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ddc01fe6-3422-5b30-91a7-0070ab16975a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541222 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186541083 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
